{
  "info": {
    "name": "Zonic Agent Builder API",
    "description": "Agent Workflow Builder API (:8000) plus the pgfoundation data gateway (:8600) it reads and writes through.\n\nRun **Health → Readiness** first: it fails fast if the gateway or the database is not reachable, which is the usual cause of everything else returning 502.\n\n**Import a package** writes the returned root id into the `ID` collection variable, so every request below it targets the workflow you just imported.\n\nFull notes: docs/curl-reference.md in the repository.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "API",
      "value": "http://localhost:8000",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "GW",
      "value": "http://localhost:8600",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "DS",
      "value": "tsdb",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Must equal PG_GATEWAY_DATASOURCE and the datasource name in the gateway's config. Check with 'Gateway → List datasources'."
    },
    {
      "key": "SCHEMA",
      "value": "agent_builder",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "ID",
      "value": "935e5116-b512-4434-82b9-bba32de3d3f8",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Set automatically by 'Import a package'."
    },
    {
      "key": "TOKEN",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "A Cognito ID token of the builder's user pool (the UI's session, or `aws cognito-idp initiate-auth`). Every /api/v1 request sends it as a bearer token."
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Liveness",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{API}}/health",
              "host": [
                "{{API}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "description": "200 while the process is up. Never touches the gateway."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Readiness",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{API}}/health/ready",
              "host": [
                "{{API}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health",
                "ready"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Calls the gateway's own /ready. 503 when the data path is unreachable. Run this first."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"data path is reachable\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql(\"ready\");",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "auth": {
        "type": "bearer",
        "bearer": [
          {
            "key": "token",
            "value": "{{TOKEN}}",
            "type": "string"
          }
        ]
      },
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Who am I (signed-in user)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{API}}/api/v1/me",
              "host": [
                "{{API}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "me"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The user the bearer token belongs to. 401 without a valid token of the builder's own pool."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Agents",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List agents",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{API}}/api/v1/agents",
              "host": [
                "{{API}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "agents"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Reads v_agent_summary. Node and edge counts are computed in SQL, not in Python."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Import a package (multipart)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{API}}/api/v1/agents/import-package",
              "host": [
                "{{API}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "agents",
                "import-package"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Pick the two files in the Body tab before sending — Postman cannot store file paths in an exported collection.\n\nRoot, children and relationships land in ONE procedure call, so a failed import leaves nothing behind.\n\nOn success the root id is saved to {{ID}}.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "agent_file",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": [],
                  "description": "Required. Select tests/fixtures/agent.json."
                },
                {
                  "key": "sub_agents_file",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": [],
                  "description": "Optional. tests/fixtures/sub_agents.json."
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"import created the package\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
                  "});",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "    var body = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"ID\", body.root_agent_id);",
                  "    console.log(\"ID set to \" + body.root_agent_id",
                  "        + \" — \" + body.sub_agent_ids.length + \" sub-agents, \"",
                  "        + body.relationship_count + \" relationships, \"",
                  "        + body.warnings.length + \" warning(s)\");",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Import a package (JSON)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "content-type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{API}}/api/v1/agents/import-package",
              "host": [
                "{{API}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "agents",
                "import-package"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Same endpoint, JSON instead of multipart. Easier to script.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"agent_data\": {\n    \"agenticWorkflowId\": \"{{ID}}\",\n    \"name\": \"demo\",\n    \"displayName\": \"Demo Workflow\",\n    \"nodes\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"n1\",\n        \"type\": \"start\",\n        \"name\": \"Start\",\n        \"config\": {}\n      }\n    ],\n    \"edges\": []\n  },\n  \"sub_agents_data\": null\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get one agent",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{API}}/api/v1/agents/{{ID}}",
              "host": [
                "{{API}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "agents",
                "{{ID}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Reads v_agent_detail. Returns the agent's own document — raw_json with the first-class fields overlaid, so unknown keys (createdBy, originalBpc, freezeRelease) survive."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Save (partial patch)",
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "content-type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{API}}/api/v1/agents/{{ID}}",
              "host": [
                "{{API}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "agents",
                "{{ID}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Calls sp_agent_workflow_save: agent, chip and relationships in one transaction.\n\nKeys you omit keep their stored value. Omitting `nodes` leaves the relationship edges alone — the canvas has not changed, so neither have they. Sending `\"nodes\": []` is a real edit and DOES clear them.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"displayName\": \"Renamed from Postman\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"saved\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql(\"saved\");",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test(\"a partial save keeps the relationships\", function () {",
                  "    // Regression guard: deriving edges from the request body",
                  "    // used to delete all of them on a rename.",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().relationshipCount).to.be.a(\"number\");",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Save (replace the canvas)",
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "content-type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{API}}/api/v1/agents/{{ID}}",
              "host": [
                "{{API}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "agents",
                "{{ID}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Sending `nodes` replaces the canvas and rebuilds the relationship edges from it.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"nodes\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"n1\",\n      \"type\": \"start\",\n      \"name\": \"Start\",\n      \"config\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"n2\",\n      \"type\": \"llm\",\n      \"name\": \"LLM_1\",\n      \"config\": {\n        \"model\": \"claude-sonnet-4-6\"\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"edges\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e1\",\n      \"source\": \"n1\",\n      \"target\": \"n2\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Relationship map",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{API}}/api/v1/agents/{{ID}}/relationships",
              "host": [
                "{{API}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "agents",
                "{{ID}}",
                "relationships"
              ]
            },
            "description": "One read of v_agent_relationship_detail, child details included. The Django version issued an extra query per child."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Export agent",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{API}}/api/v1/agents/{{ID}}/export",
              "host": [
                "{{API}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "agents",
                "{{ID}}",
                "export"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Reads v_agent_export — the raw_json overlay, expressed once in SQL so /export and /export-package cannot disagree."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Export package",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{API}}/api/v1/agents/{{ID}}/export-package",
              "host": [
                "{{API}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "agents",
                "{{ID}}",
                "export-package"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Root agent + resolved children + relationshipMap."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Export debug package",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{API}}/api/v1/agents/{{ID}}/export-debug",
              "host": [
                "{{API}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "agents",
                "{{ID}}",
                "export-debug"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Package plus unresolved and unreferenced sub-agent warnings."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Create snapshot",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "content-type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{API}}/api/v1/agents/{{ID}}/snapshots",
              "host": [
                "{{API}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "agents",
                "{{ID}}",
                "snapshots"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Built from the persisted row, not from this request — a snapshot always reflects what is stored.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"comment\": \"before edit\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Enable semantic search",
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "content-type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{API}}/api/v1/agents/{{ID}}",
              "host": [
                "{{API}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "agents",
                "{{ID}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Run this before Embed, which returns 400 while semantic search is off.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"semanticSearchEnabled\": true,\n  \"semanticDomain\": \"energy\",\n  \"semanticKeywords\": \"energy, meters, consumption\",\n  \"semanticUseCases\": \"Compare energy usage across sites\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Embed",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{API}}/api/v1/agents/{{ID}}/embed",
              "host": [
                "{{API}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "agents",
                "{{ID}}",
                "embed"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Generates the vector from the PERSISTED state and stores it via sp_agent_embedding_store.\n\n400 when semantic search is disabled for the workflow. Needs EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=bedrock with working AWS credentials; set it to `fake` to exercise the path offline."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Not found (error shape)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{API}}/api/v1/agents/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
              "host": [
                "{{API}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "agents",
                "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
              ]
            },
            "description": "One envelope for every failure: {\"error\", \"code\", \"traceId\"}. traceId is echoed in X-Request-Id and forwarded to the gateway."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"404 with the standard envelope\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(404);",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql(\"not_found\");",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "auth": {
        "type": "bearer",
        "bearer": [
          {
            "key": "token",
            "value": "{{TOKEN}}",
            "type": "string"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Registry",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Node types",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{API}}/api/v1/node-types",
              "host": [
                "{{API}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "node-types"
              ]
            },
            "description": "17 node types. Prefers v_node_type_active and falls back to the JSON resources when the table is empty, so it works before any seeding."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"all 17 node types\", function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().nodeTypes).to.have.lengthOf(17);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Tools",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{API}}/api/v1/tools",
              "host": [
                "{{API}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "tools"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Tool catalogue."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Option sets",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{API}}/api/v1/option-sets",
              "host": [
                "{{API}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "option-sets"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Shared select-option lists the UI renders. Served so the frontend holds none of its own."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Node semantics",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{API}}/api/v1/node-semantics",
              "host": [
                "{{API}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "node-semantics"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Which node types reference a child workflow, hand off to siblings, or fan out into branches, and where each of those lives on the node.\n\nThe canvas needs this to render handles: a Rule node draws one output per configured branch and an Agent node one per handoff target. Deriving them from the static registry alone drops those edges."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "MCP config schema",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{API}}/api/v1/mcp-config-schema",
              "host": [
                "{{API}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "mcp-config-schema"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The MCP tool configurator as a form schema: the server fields, the three tool kinds (database, api, function) with their sections, defaults, conditionals and validation flags, plus the parameter-row and cache-key editors.\n\nThe UI renders whatever this declares, so adding a field to a tool kind is an edit to resources/mcp_config.json and no frontend change."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ],
      "auth": {
        "type": "bearer",
        "bearer": [
          {
            "key": "token",
            "value": "{{TOKEN}}",
            "type": "string"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Workflows",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Validate",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "content-type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{API}}/api/v1/workflows/validate",
              "host": [
                "{{API}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "workflows",
                "validate"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Pure computation, no database.\n\nThis body deliberately trips two checks: the tool node has no toolName (error) and the edge points at a node that does not exist (warning).\n\nnode_count and edge_count are snake_case — the UI reads those names.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"agenticWorkflowId\": \"11111111-2222-3333-4444-555555555555\",\n  \"name\": \"demo\",\n  \"nodes\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"n1\",\n      \"type\": \"start\",\n      \"name\": \"Start\",\n      \"config\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"n2\",\n      \"type\": \"tool\",\n      \"name\": \"T\",\n      \"config\": {}\n    }\n  ],\n  \"edges\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e1\",\n      \"source\": \"n1\",\n      \"target\": \"ghost\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
